# =============================================================================================
# Projective — Environment Variable Contract (template)
#
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.development` / `.env.production`) and fill in real values LOCALLY.
# `.gitignore` ignores `.env` and `.env.*` and un-ignores THIS file — it is the only one that is
# ever committed, and it must never contain a real credential.
#
# Canonical spec: documentation/architecture/SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md §Environment Variable Contract.
# The only server-side reader is packages/backend/core/env.ts (`serverEnv()`); islands never read
# the environment. Everything else here is consumed by supabase/config.toml or by a deferred live
# path that names its key in code.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO VALUE CONVENTIONS. THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE.
#
#   1. Every SECRET is `XXXX-XXXX` (root CLAUDE.md §6). A real key is never committed. If you find
#      one here, it is already burned — rotate it, do not just delete the line.
#
#   2. Every `*_BACKEND_LIVE` gate carries its literal default, `false`. These are BOOLEANS parsed
#      as `(value ?? "false").toLowerCase() === "true"`, so `XXXX-XXXX` there is not a redacted
#      secret — it is a value that silently parses as `false` while LOOKING configured, which is
#      the worst of both.
#
# A variable that is absent and a variable that is empty are the same thing to `serverEnv()`
# (`firstEnv` treats a falsy read as unset), and an unset gate is off. So it is always safe to
# leave a line at its placeholder; the corresponding feature simply serves its fixture path.
# =============================================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `development` | `production`. Drives log verbosity and safety rails — NOT persistence (see
# LOGGING_BACKEND_LIVE, which is the orthogonal switch).
DENO_ENV=development

# Public base URL. Used to build absolute links in emails, OAuth callbacks and share URLs, so it
# must match the origin the browser actually reaches — a mismatch here produces callbacks that
# resolve to the wrong host and share links that are correct but unclickable.
APP_URL=http://localhost:8000


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (database & auth)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=XXXX-XXXX

# The anon / publishable key. RLS-scoped and used WITH a user's JWT — safe to reach the browser.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=XXXX-XXXX

# ⚠️ The service-role key BYPASSES RLS entirely. Server-only: Edge Functions and the fat service
# layer's `getServiceClient()`. It must never be sent to the client, logged, or read by an island.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=XXXX-XXXX


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (sign-in OAuth) — GoTrue owns this and retains NO API token
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consumed by supabase/config.toml `[auth.external.google]`. This grant authenticates a person; it
# does NOT authorize the platform to call Google on their behalf later. That is the separate
# consent in the next block — the distinction is load-bearing (Decision #56 §(c)).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=XXXX-XXXX
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX

# Other sign-in providers configured in config.toml but shipping DISABLED.
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_APPLE_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX
SUPABASE_AUTH_SMS_TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=XXXX-XXXX


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integrations — connection OAuth (calendar + conferencing)
#
# A SEPARATE consent that stores a long-lived API grant in integrations.connection_secrets.
# Never share a client id or a token store with the sign-in credentials above: sign-in is
# "who are you", a connection is "act at this third party as me", and conflating them means
# revoking one silently revokes the other.
# Each provider ships DISABLED (`integrations.providers.is_enabled = false`) until its credentials
# exist — enabling one is an operator decision, not a migration side effect.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_INTEGRATION_CLIENT_ID=XXXX-XXXX
GOOGLE_INTEGRATION_CLIENT_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX
MICROSOFT_INTEGRATION_CLIENT_ID=XXXX-XXXX
MICROSOFT_INTEGRATION_CLIENT_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX
ZOOM_CLIENT_ID=XXXX-XXXX
ZOOM_CLIENT_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX
ZOOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integrations — storage connectors (asset management)
#
# The mounted drives behind /files. Google Drive reuses GOOGLE_INTEGRATION_* above (ONE connection
# carrying two capabilities: `storage` + `calendar`) — do not add a second Google client here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DROPBOX_CLIENT_ID=XXXX-XXXX
DROPBOX_CLIENT_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX
FRAMEIO_CLIENT_ID=XXXX-XXXX
FRAMEIO_CLIENT_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX

# S3-compatible object storage (AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2, MinIO, Wasabi …) — the one
# connector with NO authorization server, so its credential is a static key pair rather than an
# OAuth grant (`integrations.providers.auth_scheme = 'aws_sigv4'`).
#
# ⚠️ Endpoint / region / bucket / prefix / path-style are NOT secrets and do NOT belong here. They
# are PER-CONNECTION and live in `integrations.user_connections.config`, which is projected to the
# client through `v_my_connections` precisely so the settings screen can answer "which bucket did I
# actually mount?". Anything written into that column reaches the browser on the next read.
#
# ⚠️ Distinct from the S3_HOST / S3_REGION / S3_ACCESS_KEY / S3_SECRET_KEY block below, which is
# Supabase Storage's OWN backing store. Same vendor, unrelated purpose. Do not merge them.
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=XXXX-XXXX
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=XXXX-XXXX


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Link safety (asset management)
#
# The reputation feed a pasted link's verdict is drawn from. The provider is not yet chosen; the
# key is read at CALL time and never inlined (packages/backend/services/files/link-scan.ts).
#
# Link ingest is the most dangerous path in the hub — the server fetches a URL a stranger chose —
# and stays behind FILES_BACKEND_LIVE regardless of whether this key is set. Setting it does not
# open the outbound fetch; only the gate does.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LINK_SAFETY_API_KEY=XXXX-XXXX


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe (finance)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=XXXX-XXXX
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=XXXX-XXXX
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=XXXX-XXXX


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cryptography
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 32-byte hex for Edge Function / Vault encryption.
ENCRYPTION_KEY=XXXX-XXXX

# The KMS key alias the token vault wraps per-secret data keys (DEKs) under.
#
# ⚠️ UNRESOLVED CONTRADICTION — do not silently pick a side (Decision #59; see
# SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md §Asset Management → The token vault). ENCRYPTION_KEY is ONE symmetric
# process-wide secret; the `integrations` schema was built for a KMS ENVELOPE
# (`connection_secrets.key_id` exists precisely because the wrapping key is external and
# rotatable). If ENCRYPTION_KEY is authoritative, `key_id` is decoration and rotation is a
# full-table rewrite. If the envelope is authoritative, ENCRYPTION_KEY must be removed here or
# redefined as a local-development KEK never used in production. A human decides.
KMS_KEY_ALIAS=XXXX-XXXX


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase CLI / config.toml only (local stack) — not read by serverEnv()
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase Studio's AI assistant. Optional; leave unset to disable.
OPENAI_API_KEY=XXXX-XXXX

# Supabase Storage's own S3 backing store (`[storage.experimental]`). See the warning in the
# storage-connector block above: this is NOT the S3 file connector.
S3_HOST=XXXX-XXXX
S3_REGION=XXXX-XXXX
S3_ACCESS_KEY=XXXX-XXXX
S3_SECRET_KEY=XXXX-XXXX


# =============================================================================================
# Backend live gates — BOOLEANS, default `false`
#
# Each flips exactly ONE fat service in packages/backend/services/ from its deterministic fixture
# path to its live Supabase path. They are twelve separate switches rather than one because the
# accidents they prevent are different in kind: a half-wired READ returns wrong data, a half-wired
# WRITE corrupts real rows, a half-wired MONEY mutation moves real funds, and a half-wired
# OUTBOUND call spends someone else's stored credential at a third party.
#
# Read by packages/backend/core/env.ts; predicates live in core/supabase.ts (`isXBackendLive()`),
# except `isWorkspaceBackendLive()`, which sits beside its own service.
# =============================================================================================

# Reads
AUTH_BACKEND_LIVE=false
EXPLORE_BACKEND_LIVE=false
PROJECTS_BACKEND_LIVE=false
PROFILE_BACKEND_LIVE=false
MESSAGING_BACKEND_LIVE=false

# Writes
NEWSLETTER_BACKEND_LIVE=false
CATALOGUE_BACKEND_LIVE=false
WORKSPACE_BACKEND_LIVE=false

# Persistence of the production error/warn ingest. Orthogonal to DENO_ENV: this gates PERSISTENCE,
# DENO_ENV gates VERBOSITY.
LOGGING_BACKEND_LIVE=false

# ⚠️ Money. Gates the /wallet write path (top-up · withdraw · transfer · distribute · fund-escrow ·
# recurring · payout). Defaults off even where other backends are live.
FINANCE_BACKEND_LIVE=false

# ⚠️ Stored bytes and REACH. Gates /files: a signed upload ticket authorises a real object write,
# and a share link is a bearer capability that cannot be un-forwarded once it leaks. Also gates the
# outbound link-safety fetch (SSRF surface — see LINK_SAFETY_API_KEY above).
FILES_BACKEND_LIVE=false

# ⚠️ Third-party action. Gates the connector subsystem: the OAuth consent handshake, the KMS
# envelope, and every outbound drive call. SEPARATE from FILES_BACKEND_LIVE on purpose — the two
# share a screen but not a trust model, and one flag would make "turn on the file hub" silently
# mean "start acting at Google Drive on behalf of every connected user". With this off, the token
# vault's `seal()` REFUSES rather than returning a reversible encoding, so no credential can be
# written in a form that would survive the flip as plaintext.
INTEGRATIONS_BACKEND_LIVE=false
